title: SeaWhipCoralNode
position: -702,-12
---

<<declare $SWCoralPoints = 0>>
<<declare $Speaker = "none">>

<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
You swim near the seabed, on the prowl for a new adventure, when you come across the oddest of creatures
A coral!

You find yourself face to face with a dazzling superstar. Its tresses sway hypnotically in the sea current, a vibrant shade of vermillion.
When it speaks, its melodious voice puts you in a trance.

<<set $Speaker to "SeaWhipCoral">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
Sea Whip Coral: Helloooo, sailor! Come to admire the view, or is there something I can help you with?

<<set $Speaker to "Player">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
-> You: Pardon my intrusion, I simply had to stop and stare at what a mesmerising shade of red you are.
    <<set $SWCoralPoints += 1>>
    <<update_coral_points_display>>
    The coral is rather taken aback by your forwardness, its already rosy shade darkens with a blush.
    Good job. It seems that you have managed to fluster the bold coral.
    <<set $Speaker to "Player">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    Sea Whip Coral: Oh! Well- uh...thank you!
-> You: Woah.. I've never seen a red seaweed before!
    <<set $Speaker to "SeaWhipCoral">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    <<GiveGift SW_Coral>>
    Sea Whip Coral: SEAWEED?! SEA?! WEED?!
    Sea Whip Coral: How DARE you call me a weed when I am a beautiful, majestic CORAL!
    Sea Whip Coral flashes its soft vermilion branches at you, looking not unlike a great tree swaying in the wind.
    Sea Whip Coral: BEHOLD.
    <<set $Speaker to "Player">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    You: I'm sorry, I was unaware of the existence of such a beautiful coral!
   
<<set $Speaker to "SeaWhipCoral">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>> 
Sea Whip Coral: Look closer! Within me, each little polyp holds eight feathery, saw-toothed tentacles.
You squint your eyes, bringing your angular face closer to her majestic red branches.
True to its word, the tentacles emerge and sweeps their adoring fans of the plankton and microscopic particles right up into themselves.
Sea Whip Coral: I have many adoring fans, though I do attract a particular kind of company. Can you guess what species my fanbase is mostly made off?
-> You: Black sea bass?
    <<set $SWCoralPoints += 1>>
    <<update_coral_points_display>>
    <<set $Speaker to "SeaWhipCoral">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>> 
    Sea Whip Coral: Oh, so you noticed them? Yes, those are black sea bass. They know a good home when they see one!
    Sea Whip Coral: I'm flattered you're paying such close attention. A star has to appreciate a devoted audience, after all.
-> You: Stingrays?
    Sea Whip Coral: Stingrays?! You must be joking. Those flat, sandy creatures prefer to skulk around the mud and rocks.
    Sea Whip Coral: But I suppose I shouldn't expect a bunch of literal bottom dwellers to have any true appreciation for my beauty anyway.
    
You notice the sea whip coral, its long crimson strands swaying and whipping with the ocean current, moving in a slow, rhythmic dance.
Sea Whip Coral: As a suspension feeder, I am eating plankton. 
Sea Whip Coral: People would pay to witness this, but you are seeing it for free, so etch it into your memory!
Sea Whip Coral: WITNESS MY GREATNESS!!
-> You give a faintly disgusted look.
    <<if $SWCoralPoints >= 1>>
        <<set $SWCoralPoints -= 1>>
        <<update_coral_points_display>>
    <<endif>>
    You thought Sea Whip Coral would be busy looking, but it steals a quick look at you and sees your reaction.
    Sea Whip Coral: Oh.
    Sea Whip Coral: That look.
    Sea Whip Coral: I suppose not everyone appreciates fine dining. I didn't know why I expected you to be any different from the rest.
    The coral's face shutters, and it seems to lose all interest in conversing with you for the day.
    <<returnToHome>>
-> You state quietly in amazement and awe.
    <<set $SWCoralPoints += 1>>
    <<update_coral_points_display>>
    Sea Whip turns around and stares at you. A small sincere smile lights up their face. 
    This was a smile unlike their usual haughty one, aimed at your candid acceptance and fascination with their being. 
    Sea Whip Coral: Perhaps...we could be friends! You seem rather alright...for a fish.
    <<set $Speaker to "Player">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    You: I would love to be friends!
    <<set $Speaker to "None">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    The coral's sparkle fades to a sleepy shimmer, like a star dozing off after the show. The reef returns to its peaceful rhythm. The conversation comes to an end.
    <<returnToHome>>
===

title: GroovedBrainCoralNode
position: 98,-12
---
You swim near the seabed, on the prowl for a new adventure, when you come across the oddest of creatures
A coral!

<<set $Speaker to "Player">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
You: Whoa, what a cute parrot fish!

You get closer to take a clearer look when someone interrupted you.

<<set $Speaker to "None">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
Grooved Brain Coral: That’s actually a Wrasse, not a parrot fish.

<<set $Speaker to "GroovedBrainCoral">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
said a nearby coral.

<<set $Speaker to "None">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
You looked away embarrassingly.

<<set $Speaker to "Player">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
You: Nope, I didn't say anything.

Seeing your face red with embarrassment, it smirked at you. 

<<set $Speaker to "GroovedBrainCoral">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
Grooved Brain Coral: It’s ok to be embarrassed, after all, I, Grooved Brain Coral, am here to educate the masses.

<<set $Speaker to "None">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
That comment irked you. Naturally, you decided that rage baiting was the mature response.

<<set $Speaker to "Player">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
You: You are wrong, that fish is MOST definitely a parrot fish!

<<set $Speaker to "GroovedBrainCoral">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
Grooved brain Coral let out a laugh of disbelief.

Grooved Brain Coral: Erm, actually that’s a wrasse. Though they both hold similarities, the main difference is that parrot fish have a distinctive beak-like mouth for scraping algae off coral.

<<set $Speaker to "Player">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
You: Source?

<<set $Speaker to "GroovedBrainCoral">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
Grooved Brain Coral: I would know... my colony never recovered after a hungry parrot fish came through.
-> Whoa, things just got dark...
    It ignored your comment and started rambling again. 
    Grooved Brain Coral: That is why I know that is definitely a wrasse. Speaking of which, where has it gone off to?
-> Can that little guy really be the cause of that?
    <<set $SWCoralPoints += 5>>
    <<update_coral_points_display>>
    Grooved Brain Coral: Without a doubt! I'd recognize a wrasse anywhere. Unless... no, wait... it had the... beak... thing... Actually, forget I said that. It was a wrasse. Final answer.

<<set $Speaker to "Player">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
You: Oh hey, the Wrasse is back and its nibbling on you. That’s so cute, look at it go!

<<set $Speaker to "GroovedBrainCoral">>
<<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
The coral looked up. Lo and behold, the fish was gobbling away. It let out a piercing shriek.
-> Let the fish continue nibbling.
    You stood by and watched as the Grooved Brain Coral was helplessly nibbled by the fish. Once it had its fill, the fish swam away.
    The coral stared blankly into the distance, evidently done with this conversation... and perhaps with you as well.
    <<returnToHome>>
-> Eat the fish
    <<set $SWCoralPoints += 5>>
    <<update_coral_points_display>>
    You gobbled the fish up, saving the coral from becoming the fish’s next meal.
    Grooved Brain Coral: Thank you... I suppose I owe you one. And yes, before you say anything, that was definitely a wrasse. I refuse to discuss the matter any further.
    The coral cleared its throat. 
    Grooved Brain Coral: Come back and visit me sometime. There's still plenty about the reef for you to learn... even if your fish identification skills need work.
    <<returnToHome>>
===
